      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Cynthia “Cinde” Wirth is a seventh-generation resident of Bartholomew County, Indiana (Columbus), where she raised her family. As a scientist and educator, she spent more than a decade teaching high school biology and environmental science. Cinde inspired her students to take their STEM skills out of the classroom by creating and teaching a marine biology research based study abroad program on the Caribbean island of Bonaire. In 2018-2019, she served as a congressional fellow in Washington, D.C., learning to write science and education policy while navigating bipartisan challenges. A first-generation college graduate, in 2025 Cinde earned her Ph.D in cultural and educational policy from Ball State University, proudly capping off a winding path through her own education journey.",
